<article class="py-16 lg:py-24 bg-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5">
    <img
      src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1499750310107-5fef28a66643?w=900&q=80&auto=format&fit=crop"
      alt="Laptop reviewing a manufacturer&#x27;s website"
      class="w-full rounded-2xl object-cover mb-10"
      style="max-height:380px"
      loading="lazy"
      width="900" height="450">
    <div class="prose max-w-none">
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-8">Industrial buyers rarely find a manufacturer through a website. They usually arrive with a part number, a recommendation from a distributor or a spec from an engineer, and they come to confirm, download and ask for a price. If your site makes that hard, they call a competitor whose site doesn't. Count how many of these 12 points your site passes.</p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">Products and specs</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-8 space-y-3">
        <li><strong>Every product has its own page</strong> with the specs buyers filter by: sizes, ratings, materials, standards.</li>
        <li><strong>Spec sheets and cut sheets download as PDF</strong>, with the current revision and date on them.</li>
        <li><strong>Submittal documents are easy to gather:</strong> spec sheet, installation instructions, warranty and listings in one place.</li>
        <li><strong>Part numbers are searchable</strong> from the site search, including old numbers that customers still use.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">Getting a quote</h2>
      <ol start="5" class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-8 space-y-3">
        <li><strong>The quote form asks the right questions:</strong> part numbers, quantities, delivery location and date, not just name and email.</li>
        <li><strong>Where to buy is clear:</strong> direct sales, distributors by region, or both.</li>
        <li><strong>Phone and email are on every page</strong>, and someone answers the same business day.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">Trust</h2>
      <ol start="8" class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-8 space-y-3">
        <li><strong>Industries and applications are explained</strong> with real photos of your products installed, not stock images.</li>
        <li><strong>Certifications and listings are accurate:</strong> only the ones each product actually holds, ideally with the certificate or listing number.</li>
        <li><strong>Company basics are visible:</strong> location, years in business, capacity, who to contact.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">Reach</h2>
      <ol start="11" class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-8 space-y-3">
        <li><strong>Key pages and documents exist in Spanish</strong> if your installers, crews or counter staff work in Spanish.</li>
        <li><strong>It works on a phone at a job site:</strong> pages load fast, PDFs open, and each product page has its own title and description so Google can index it.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">How to read your score</h2>
      <ul class="checklist mb-8">
        <li><span><strong>10 to 12:</strong> your site supports sales. Focus on getting more of the right people to it.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>7 to 9:</strong> you are losing quotes in specific places. Fix the missing points in the first two groups first.</span></li>
        <li><span><strong>6 or fewer:</strong> buyers are probably calling or emailing for information the site should give them, or going elsewhere.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">What to fix first</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-8">Start with points 2 and 5. Current <a href="/en/solutions/spec-sheets/" style="color:var(--primary)">spec sheets</a> that download in one click and a quote form that collects part numbers and quantities will do more for sales than a redesign. Then work on product pages and <a href="/en/solutions/product-content/" style="color:var(--primary)">product content</a>, and when the whole site needs to change, see our <a href="/en/services/web-design-treasure-coast/" style="color:var(--primary)">industrial website design</a>.</p>
